# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo, so pin them.
#
# `test/build-gate.test.mjs` compares the COMMITTED bytes of `client.js` and
# `lib/*.js` with the bytes a fresh build emits, and the bundler always emits LF.
# Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which converts text files to
# CRLF on checkout — on such a clone the gate can never pass, no matter how fresh
# the artifacts are. It cost a red CI leg on 2026-10-17 (the first run of the
# Windows matrix leg; the Linux leg is immune because it checks out LF).
#
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout LF everywhere, which is what the blobs already are.
# Do NOT "fix" a red gate by committing CRLF artifacts: the next `npm run build`
# on any machine rewrites them as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A PNG is not text; keep git from ever looking inside it.
*.png binary
